# PoC: publish zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 (and wl_drm when possible) without a DrmDevice
#
# Status: proof of concept, NOT meant for upstream. This patch applies on top of
# the lfdevs series in this directory - it edits code introduced by
# backends-anland-Add-support-for-running-without-a-DR.patch - so it must stay
# after that one in series.ci.
#
# Why this is needed
# ------------------
# In Anland/surfaceless mode (ANLAND_NO_DRM_DEVICE=1) there is no DrmDevice, so
# AbstractEglBackend::initWayland() cannot derive a dma-buf format table from a
# scanout device. The lfdevs series already added an "else" branch for that case,
# but it only does something when EglDisplay::nonExternalOnlySupportedDrmFormats()
# is non-empty. Under surfaceless KGSL/Turnip EGL, EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import
# (_modifiers) is not exposed, so that query returns nothing, the tranche list
# stays empty, and zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 - created lazily by
# WaylandServer::linuxDmabuf() together with setSupportedFormatsWithModifiers() -
# is never instantiated. Clients see no dma-buf global and stay on wl_shm.
#
# What this patch does
# --------------------
# 1. abstract_egl_backend.cpp: adds fallbackDmaBufFormats(), a static linear-only
#    table (ARGB8888/XRGB8888/ABGR8888/XBGR8888/ABGR2101010/XRGB2101010, each with
#    DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR).
# 2. initWayland(), no-DRM branch: always create the
#    LinuxDmaBufV1ClientBufferIntegration, register the render backend and call
#    setSupportedFormatsWithModifiers() - using the fallback table when EGL
#    reported no formats. Both calls must happen before any client binds the
#    global, and setSupportedFormatsWithModifiers() dereferences
#    tranches.first(), so the list is never left empty. wl_drm is still only
#    advertised when EGL knows a render node: it hands the node path to clients,
#    and an empty path only makes them fail open("").
# 3. testImportBuffer(): with no DRM device and no EGL-reported formats, a
#    fallback format with a LINEAR/INVALID modifier is still passed to a real
#    eglCreateImageKHR import instead of being rejected up front. The result is
#    reported honestly - if KGSL/Turnip cannot create the EGLImage the client
#    gets zwp_linux_buffer_params_v1 failed/invalid_wl_buffer.
#
# Known limits
# ------------
# - Publishing the global plus a format list is all this PoC claims. Real buffer
#   import depends on the EGL driver: without working EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import
#   (and LINEAR modifier handling), importBufferAsImage() returns
#   EGL_NO_IMAGE_KHR and every client buffer is rejected.
# - Clients also need a way to allocate dma-bufs. QtWayland/QtQuick clients on
#   this device have no /dev/dri render node, so they cannot produce a dma-buf
#   even once the global exists. That side is out of scope here.
# - wl_drm usually will not appear: with Anland/KGSL, EGL reports no render node.
#   Expect zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 only.
# - The advertised table is not verified against the driver; it is deliberately
#   minimal (LINEAR only) so that clients cannot be led into tiled layouts.
#
# Revert
# ------
#   git apply -R zz-poc-dmabuf-without-drmdevice.patch
# or remove the last line of series.ci and rebuild.
#
# Debugging: grep the kwin log for "[dmabuf-poc]".
#
diff --git a/src/platformsupport/scenes/opengl/abstract_egl_backend.cpp b/src/platformsupport/scenes/opengl/abstract_egl_backend.cpp
index e6bc3d3..1a11258 100644
--- a/src/platformsupport/scenes/opengl/abstract_egl_backend.cpp
